---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/07-06/', manual='https://www.eppendorf.com/product-media/doc/en/330816/Centrifugation_Operating-manual_Centrifuge-5804-5804-R_Centrifuge-5810-5810-R.pdf', product='https://www.eppendorf.com/us-en/Products/Centrifugation/Multipurpose-Centrifuges/Centrifuge-5810-5810R-p-PF-240994', front='https://assets.fishersci.com/TFS-Assets/CCG/Eppendorf/product-images/155463.jpg-650.jpg';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Eppendorf 5810 R · documentary exterior and detached statics" description="Inspect the closed Eppendorf exterior and compare two unrelated planar static moment diagrams." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment ep"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/07-06/">← Equipment 07-06</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#ep-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">07-06 · DOCUMENTARY MODEL & DETACHED STATICS / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Eppendorf Centrifuge 5810 R</h2><p>Orbit the closed stationary 5810 R. On the separate teaching monitor, compare two fixed diagrams of a supported line. In the first, unequal forces produce equal opposing moments; in the second, their moments no longer cancel. Neither diagram describes the instrument.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Closed refrigerated-variant casing</h3><div id="ep-view" aria-label="Orbitable stationary Eppendorf 5810 R, closed lid and detached teaching monitor"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-ep-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-ep-view="shell">Enclosure detail</button><button data-ep-view="display">Detached monitor</button><button id="ep-cycle">Switch statics card</button></div>
<p id="ep-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal badge changes only the separate monitor. The opaque lid is fixed and the panel is inactive.</p></section>
<section><h3>Detached static moment comparison</h3><canvas id="ep-plot" width="660" height="450" aria-label="Unaffiliated statics drawing with two vertically downward forces on either side of a reference pivot"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Fixed diagram<select id="ep-case"><option value="zero">Equal opposing moments</option><option value="nonzero">Unequal opposing moments</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="ep-inspect">Inspect signed moments</button><button id="ep-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="ep-status" aria-live="polite">Choose a fixed card and read its signed moment sum.</p><output id="ep-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="ep-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="ep-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected configuration: the wider <a href={product}>refrigerated Eppendorf 5810 R</a>, not the narrower 5810 or 5804. The <a href={manual+'#page=17'}>manufacturer manual p. 17, fig. 3-1</a> supplies the three-quarter cabinet silhouette and right extension. The <a href={front}>Fisher Scientific exterior photo</a> shows the sloping face, blue button marks, lid seam and base coverage with the lid shut. <a href={manual+'#page=60'}>Manual p. 60, §10.3.1</a> gives the exact nominal dimensions and footprint depth. Individual forms and radii are inferred. No chamber, motion, or operational control is modeled.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original 3D enclosure with wider right shell and unrelated monitor"/><figcaption>Original front-quarter render, not a photo. The 5810 R's wider right housing distinguishes it from the narrower variant.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original close-up with closed lid, gray sweep and inactive front panel"/><figcaption>Original front-left comparison with the manual figure. All marks and the filled lid dot are cosmetic only.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Closed outer hull and support depth</td><td>700 W × 608 D × 345 H mm; footprint depth 536 mm</td><td>Verified in metric GLB. Local forms and radii are photo estimates.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Static card 1</td><td>+6×0.40 and −8×0.30 N·m</td><td>+2.40 and −2.40 N·m; net 0.00 N·m.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Static card 2</td><td>+6×0.40 and −7×0.30 N·m</td><td>+0.30 N·m net, counterclockwise by sign convention. Diagram does not rotate.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Original register acceptance</td><td>Rotor relationship and fraction conservation</td><td>Not implemented or run. This diagram calculates static moments only, without actual rotor geometry or movement, specimens, settings or processing.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The two unrelated cards have immutable locations in meters. Each downward force contributes <code>M = x Fᵧ</code> with positive X to the right and negative Fᵧ for down; positive moment is counterclockwise. JSON includes the authored drawing version, positions, signed values, units, and provenance. It is not a centrifuge run record or a hardware readout.</p>
<p><a href={base+'eppendorf-5810r-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'diagram-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/07-06/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.ep{max-width:76rem}.ep .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.ep section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.ep .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.ep .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.ep label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.ep input,.ep select,.ep button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.ep button{cursor:pointer}.ep button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.ep .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.ep #ep-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.ep #ep-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.ep #ep-plot,.ep img{width:100%;height:auto}.ep #ep-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.ep #ep-status.error{color:#a54a34}.ep .scroll{overflow:auto}.ep table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.ep td,.ep th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.ep figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.ep .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
